  <title>Complete search</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>General</gui><gui>Complete search</gui></guiseq> looks for
  text in every column of every table, when you do not know where something
  was written: a check number, part of a remark, a phone number.</p>

  <steps>
    <item><p>Type what to look for and press <key>Enter</key>, or click
    <gui>Search</gui>. Capitals do not matter. Searching every table can take
    a while.</p></item>
    <item><p>The results list each <gui>Table</gui> and <gui>Column</gui>
    where it was <gui>Found</gui>, and how many results there are.</p></item>
    <item><p>Double click a result to see the whole record it was found
    in. A blank cell there has no value, and a tick box with no value shows
    unticked.</p></item>
  </steps>

  <section id="generator">
  <title>Searching for several words</title>
  <p>The search text is a regular expression. To build one without knowing
  how, click <gui>Search generator</gui>. Click <gui>Add word</gui> for each
  word and type it into the list, choose the <gui>Type of search :</gui>, such
  as <gui>find ALL of these partial words</gui>, and click
  <gui>Generate</gui>. The expression is put in the search box. <gui>Delete
  word</gui> and <gui>Clear all</gui> remove words.</p>
  </section>

</page>
